# Summary

The pipeline is intentionally staged so that downstream results cannot modify upstream preprocessing or clustering decisions.

In simplified form:

```text
Raw dietary data
      |
      v
LER exclusion
      |
      v
FFQ coding -> 18 food groups
      |
      v
Willett energy adjustment
      |
      v
Z-standardisation
      |
      v
Outcome-independent dietary clustering
      |
      v
Frozen Food-diverse / Food-limited profiles
      |
      +---------------------------------------+
      |                                       |
      v                                       v
Baseline molecular panels                Clinical covariates
      |
      v
Feature QC
      |
      v
Cytokines: log1p
Small molecules/lipoproteins: configured raw scale
      |
      v
Median imputation
      |
      v
PCA + parallel analysis + Hotelling T²
      |
      v
Frozen omics preprocessing/outlier flags
      |
      +-----------------------------+
      |                             |
      v                             v
Within-profile biomarkers       Multivariate/deep-dive analyses
      |                             |
      v                             v
Wilcoxon + Cliff's delta        PCA / PERMANOVA / PERMDISP
BH-FDR                         Cytokine heterogeneity
Logistic adjustment            Micronutrient associations
                               Cytokine FCM subgroups
                               Interaction analyses
                               Longitudinal case series
```

The overall design maintains a strict separation between:

```text
dietary profile discovery,
molecular preprocessing,
primary biomarker testing,
and exploratory downstream analyses.
```

This reduces outcome-driven analytical decisions and preserves traceability throughout the thesis workflow.